/* ===== agent B b012: game-packet transport (PS3 1.19 game sockets, packet pump, connection base, time sync) and the
 * NetUpdate net-time block =====
 * Map (PS3 1.19; PS4 kept the connection entries 0x17f31b0 and the game halves of each entry's event connection, vtable
 * 0x16d2e90: [0] record alloc 0x6a8180, [1] ReadPacket 0x6a8450, [2] WritePacket 0x6a94a0, [3] acked 0x6a9ec0, [4] lost
 * 0x6aa030 = PS3 vt+0/+4/+8/+0xc/+0x10, and the reset f_2bf500 = 0x6aa150; it lost everything that moves packets):
 *   game sockets 0x122b7ac (UDP 3233, game traffic) / 0x122bc04 (UDP 3232, the ND master-server channel): f_948bac (reset),
 *     f_949190 (open: socket, non-blocking, bind), f_949438 (recvfrom), f_948bb0 (sendto), f_948f98 (flush), f_94914c (close).
 *     Opened by NetInit (1.19 0x2973b0..0x2973fc, LAN branch, before the connection manager; a failure fails NetInit,
 *     0xa0f86214), closed by NetShutdown f_280f68 (0x2811a4 / 0x2811b4).
 *   pump f_287500 (from the net frame f_2956dc, 0x295844): receive loop (type byte 0 data -> connection base read + game
 *     ReadPacket, 2 time request -> 3 reply, 3 time reply -> sync sample, 4 ping -> 5 pong, 5 pong -> round trip), then per
 *     connection entry with an address: drop expired unreliable events f_2be9a4, ping every 10 s, data every 0.05 s when
 *     due (f_2be144, 2 s keep-alive): {0, connection base write + game WritePacket, voice flag}; flush f_948f98.
 *   connection base (biglib net, PS4 has only the game halves): read f_947d8c + f_947a14 (header: data flag, 11-bit sequence,
 *     10-bit ack, 32-bit ack bits; acked / lost records -> vt[3] / vt[4]), write f_947e44 + f_947ca4 (window of 31 records,
 *     record from vt[0], game write vt[2]), timeout f_947d28. PS3 sub-object fields +4.. -> PS4 +8.. (8-byte vtable):
 *     sequence out +8, in +0xc, ack bits +0x14, last acked +0x18, per-sequence words +0x1c, record tag +0xa0, send time +0xa4,
 *     receive time +0xa8, lost / acked counts +0xac / +0xb0, bytes out / in +0xb4 / +0xb8, record list +0x100 / +0x108
 *     (record: +0 tag, +4 sequence, +8 next, +0x10 events), event queues +0x110 (reliable) / +0x120 (unreliable) / +0x138
 *     (received), keep-alive timer +0x164 (all checked against 0x6aa150 / 0x6a9ec0 / 0x6aa030 / 0x6a94a0 / 0x7336e0).
 *   time sync: request (f_286644's 0x286bc4 block: every 0.1..0.4 s until 8 samples, from a guest to the match host) and
 *     reply / sample handling in the pump; 8 samples sorted by half round trip (0x1188a48 = f_280cd8), net time = now +
 *     the mean offset of the 4 best; reset f_280d28 where PS3 calls it: f_2bc124 (= PS4 0x6a6690, kind 75) and the
 *     f_2bd584 state-0xf case after f_2fc150(0/1) (= PS4 0x6a6900 at 0x6a6e68, kind 76).
 *   net time (NetUpdate f_292b98 0x292bb8..0x292cb0, approved option (a); PS3 runs NetUpdate only while net +5 is set, frame
 *     loop 0x3ff90..0x3ffa0, 0x123ef8d = PS4 0x17d5c61): unless the pause byte 0x122c1a1 (PS4 0x17c3571) is set, accumulator
 *     0x122c1a4 (0x17c3574) += frame dt (0x11dfdb0+0xc = PS4 *(0x1b24b98)+0xc) x net-time scale 0x11cfc40 (= the cinema
 *     speed 0x16e716c) x 300 x the net clock's rate (+4); pause byte = 0x122c1a2 (0x17c3572); whole ticks move into
 *     0x122c1a8 (0x17c3578). Then Clock::Set (f_954308 = 0x1196cb0)(*net clock pointer 0x122c1ac = 0x17c3580, &net time, 1)
 *     and the clock's rate +4 = 0, so the engine's Clock::Update (f_9548d8 = 0x1197090, which advances by dt x rate) leaves
 *     it alone until the next NetUpdate. The net clock is engine clock 7 on both (1.19 f_296134 0x296154: 0x11dff7c =
 *     0x11dfdb0 + 68 + 7 x 56; PS4 0x17b4c98 since f002), or the helper-owned clock with U3MP_NET_CLOCK=0.
 *     KEPT SWITCH (rate): Clock::Set with flag 1 writes rate 1.0 directly and skips the property tween f_9e7ca8 (1.19
 *     0x954390; PS4 0x1196d24 the same), and the 0 stored right after stays: no 1.19 writer of clock 7's rate was found (the
 *     139 loads of the pointer 0x122c1ac, the clock array loops of stride 56, the frame update f_7ac028) and PS4 has none
 *     either (no store to 0x17b4a90+0x20c). Yet 1.19's net time does advance on the host (f_286644 0x286cc4 sends it,
 *     f_287500 0x287714 measures round trips against clock 7), so the rate the accumulator reads is effectively 1.0 there. The
 *     port reads +4 as PS3 does and uses 1.0 only while +4 still holds the 0 this block stored. U3MP_NET_TIME=0 turns the
 *     whole block (and the sync) off.
 *     The 1.19 alternate dt (frame +8 instead of +0xc while netgame +0x5534 = 0x123b2d4 is set) is not ported: 1.19 only
 *     ever clears that byte (0x309558, 0x3116c4, 0x320a30), so the branch never runs.
 * Not ported here (each has its own reason): f_2956dc's NP pieces (f_949da0 link check and 0x136e6d0 poll: online only;
 *   f_2bb528 / f_295480: NP time and NP events; f_28a4a4: NP clan-tag moderation), voice (f_39e0f0 / f_39dab4 / f_39e3ec:
 *   cellMic / cellVoice; the packet keeps PS3's "no voice" bit), the 3232 master-server decoder f_292744 (ND heartbeat
 *   replies, encrypted with key 0x137e010; nothing on a LAN sends them: packets are read and dropped), the rest of the
 *   QoS report / host migration part of the connection monitor f_286644 (never runs in 1.19: see the b013 header), the
 *   debug network simulation of f_948bb0 (loss / latency / duplicates from 0x12fd4c4, all 0 in retail), the per-player
 *   +0x454 reset at sync completion (no PS4 offset known), and the per-entry stats PS4 has no field for (they live here).
 * Wire: PS4's own bit stream (u32 words, MSB first), sent as whole words; both ends run this port.
 * Buffers: static only (t002). U3MP_NET_TIME=0 (eb[0] bit3) leaves the net clock free running (no net-time block, no sync).
 * Diagnostics eb[96..127]: [96] sockets open (bit0 3233, bit1 3232), [97] last open error, [98] packets in, [99] packets
 *   out, [100] data packets in, [101] data packets out, [102] game reads (new data), [103] records acked, [104] records
 *   lost, [105] pings sent, [106] pongs, [107] time requests answered, [108] time samples, [109] syncs completed, [110] last
 *   sync offset, [111] dropped packets (no entry / bad type), [112] 3232 packets dropped, [113] frames pumped, [114] net-time
 *   frames, [115] sync resets, [116] expired events dropped, [117] last receive size, [118] window full, [119] bytes out. */
