/* ===== agent B b014: PS3 1.19 online backend class (Naughty Dog "NetMatchmaking" client) =====
 * PS3 1.19 NetInit's online branch (worker 0x2970ec..0x2971f4, LAN byte net +4 = 0) allocates this class with
 * f_722264(0x24d60, heap 27, 8), constructs it with f_385614 (vtable 0x10f8068, 17 slots), stores it as the session manager
 * 0x125cfe4 and as the online object 0x125cfec (PS4 0x17dd768 / 0x17dd760), copies the 36-byte online id net +0x3a8 to
 * +4..+0x27 and calls slot 0. The class talks to Naughty Dog's matchmaking server over the biglib TCP socket class (the
 * same one the leaderboards use); the rooms live on that server. PS4 kept every caller of the slots (match search 0x6a6690
 * calls slot 5 with PS3's arguments, the match state machine 0x6a6900 / the party machine 0x77d270 poll the session's done /
 * result fields) but not the class. This block is the class on PS4 structures, 1:1 per slot and per message.
 *   slot 0 f_3831dc Init           PS3: connect, ClientHello 301 {online id}, ServerHello 302 (challenge), ClientHello2 326
 *                                  (proof). Here the community-server sign-in (b006, HELLO with the token) is that
 *                                  connection: Init succeeds when it is signed in. Next ping = now + 30 s.
 *   slot 1 f_3845bc Update         ping 325 every 30 s; the received messages 305 306 308 310 312 313 315 317 319 321 324
 *                                  (sizes and fields below); a lost connection returns -1 (PS3: poll error)
 *   slot 2 f_3831a0 Shutdown       PS3 closes the matchmaking socket; here the received-message buffer is dropped (the
 *                                  community connection stays up for leaderboards / friends, which use it too)
 *   slot 3 f_3835f8 AttachSession  4 bindings, session +8 = backend (f_37efe0 = PS4 0x7a2780)
 *   slot 4 f_3836c0 Create         RoomCreate 303 (232 bytes)
 *   slot 5 f_385394 Search         RoomSearch 309 (36 bytes); results arrive as 310
 *   slot 6 f_3842b0 Join           RoomJoin 304 (88 bytes)
 *   slot 7 f_3841ac Leave          RoomLeave 307 (16 bytes), room 0, ClearMembers
 *   slot 8 f_38407c SetAttr        SetAttrFlags 318 (value, mask 3) when the attribute changes
 *   slot 9 f_383fb0 Kick           Kickout 311
 *   slot 10 f_383eec Promote       Promote 316
 *   slot 11 f_383de8 RoomFlags     SetRoomFlags 320, or without a room (host) session +0x204 / +0xf0 directly
 *   slot 12 f_383c88 MemberData    session +0x12f0 / +0x12f4, MemberSetData 314
 *   slot 13 f_385540 SetAttr4      SetAttrFlags 318 (value 4 or 0, mask 4)
 *   slot 14 f_383b28 HostRank      HostRank 322 (16 + 2n bytes), or without a room session +0xe0 = 1
 *   slot 15 f_3852b4 RoomNameAuto  session name +0x20 = "%s.%lld" (online id, network time), SetRoomName 323
 *   slot 16 f_383110 RoomName      SetRoomName 323 with the session name +0x20
 * Messages (offsets as PS3; little endian here, both ends are this port and the community server; ONLINE-IFACE-C.md):
 *   301 ClientHello 48, 302 ServerHello 16, 303 RoomCreate 232, 304 RoomJoin 88, 305 RoomJoined 160 + n x 104 (member
 *   record: name[36], u16 id +36, u8 nat +38, u8 data length +39, data[64] +40), 306 MemberJoined 120, 307 RoomLeave 16,
 *   308 RoomLeft 24, 309 RoomSearch 36, 310 RoomSearchResult 16 + n x 56, 311 Kickout 16, 312 Kickedout 16, 313
 *   RoomDestroyed 16, 314 MemberSetData 80, 315 MemberUpdatedData 80, 316 Promote 16, 317 OwnerChanged 16, 318 SetAttrFlags
 *   16, 319 UpdatedAttrFlags 16, 320 SetRoomFlags 16, 321 UpdatedRoomFlags 16, 322 HostRank 16 + 2n, 323 SetRoomName 144,
 *   324 UpdatedRoomName 144, 325 Ping 4, 326 ClientHello2 8 (sizes from f_3831dc's table, numbers from the send / receive
 *   code). Each one travels as one community-server frame 0x0400 + (type - 300) (client to server, no reply) or push
 *   0xC400 + (type - 300); the payload is the message itself. The client appends pushes to the receive buffer and Update
 *   parses them exactly as PS3 parsed its TCP stream.
 * Session (PS3 -> PS4, from Session Init f_37ef48 = 0x7a2360, f_37efec = 0x7a2790, match search 0x6a6690 / 0x6a6830):
 *   +0xc pool -> +0x14, +0x10 room -> +0x18, +0x18 name[128] -> +0x20, +0x99/+0x9c create done/result -> +0xa1/+0xa4,
 *   +0xa4/+0xa8 search done/result -> +0xb0/+0xb4, +0xac/+0xb0/+0xb4 join done/result/joined -> +0xb8/+0xbc/+0xc0,
 *   +0xb8/+0xbc leave done/result -> +0xc8/+0xcc, +0xd0 rank done -> +0xe0, +0xd8 name done -> +0xe8, +0xe0 flags set ->
 *   +0xf0, +0xe8 game type -> +0xf8, +0x1f4 room flags -> +0x204, +0x1fc capacity -> +0x20c, +0x208 result count -> +0x218,
 *   +0x210 results (56 each: room +0, host name +8, +0x2c, +0x34) -> +0x220 (0x6a6830 reads +0x220 + 0x38 i), +0x16f8 host
 *   id -> +0x12e8, +0x16fc attribute -> +0x12ec, +0x1700/+0x1704 member data -> +0x12f0/+0x12f4. Session vtable callbacks
 *   PS3 vt+4k = PS4 slot k: 1 created, 2 joined, 5 lost, 6 kicked, 7 owner changed.
 * Deviations, each for a PS4 / community-server reason:
 *   - The session cookie in 303 / 304 / 309 and in 305 / 310 (PS3: the 32-bit session pointer, echoed by the server) is the
 *     binding index + 1 here (PS4 pointers are 64-bit); an unknown cookie is consumed and ignored (PS3 would use it).
 *   - Region / languages (sceNpManagerGetAccountRegion / GetMyLanguages, RoomCreate +16, RoomSearch +32): no NP account, 0.
 *   - "%s.%lld" network time (f_2bb528, NP time): the clock 3 tick count (the name only has to be unique per player).
 *   - The ND ClientHello / ServerHello / ClientHello2 handshake is the community sign-in (the server knows the profile).
 * Not ported: the per-binding room server and socket objects f_385614 builds (no online slot uses them).
 * Diagnostics eb[128..159]: [128] backend address low, [129] online NetInits, [130] Init result, [131] slot calls, [132] last
 *   slot, [133] messages sent, [134] last sent type, [135] messages received (parsed), [136] last received type, [137]
 *   pings, [138] creates, [139] joins, [140] searches, [141] leaves, [142] search results, [143] members added, [144]
 *   members removed, [145] kicked / destroyed, [146] owner changes, [147] receive buffer overflows, [148] unknown cookies,
 *   [149] Update errors (not signed in), [150] online NetInit state, [151] sign-in wait ticks. */
