/* ===== agent 1 v7.102: the level multi-all wanted for the whole MP session (PS3 1.19 Connecting f_28f800) =====
 * Airport co-op adventure kills had no kill chime. PS4 0x736a1b..0x736a3c / 0x736a78..0x736a8c (= PS3 1.19
 * 0x324088..0x3240b0 / 0x324160..0x32418c) play it on a kill: sound process 0x1007610(info, 0x845fa614, 0) + spawn
 * 0x119b250 (PS3 f_7cbb78 / f_958090); 0x845fa614 = sfx-kill-chime, the sound "kill-chime" of bank common-multi (the
 * only other copy, hud-big, is a single-player bank). common-multi is a sound bank of the level multi-all (PS3
 * dlc-patch18 pak23.txt and the overlay pak23_ps4.txt alike; also of menu-default, multi-menu and two versus Airport
 * paks). PS3 Connecting f_28f800 0x28fa34..0x28fad8 wants "net", "multi-all" and "multi-menu" as levels (f_8bb2a0 +
 * f_8b8afc, flags byte 0x50 = PS4 0x0a, keep bit set, so the match setup's want-list clear keeps them); 0x29c420 drops
 * multi-menu when the match starts, NetShutdown f_280f68 0x28132c..0x281378 drops multi-all. So on PS3 common-multi is
 * loaded in every match. PS4's Connecting page 0x672c30 is a RET stub and the eboot has no "multi-all" string; the
 * helper wanted "net" and (g001) multi-all's actors, not the level. 56 of the 57 co-op netgames (and the versus ones)
 * list multi-all in their own stage paks; the Airport co-op adventure 0x1c37ceb7 does not (same on PS3), so it alone
 * ran without common-multi (no kill chime, assist, hit markers ... of that bank) and without ss-icon-controller.
 * Port: m01_keep (every LAN/online stage_tick, outside a match) wants multi-all {hash, sid 0x240b27b8, 0, flags 0x0a}
 * as the helper wants "net", and puts the keep bit on an entry that lacks it; m01_drop (NetShutdown level step) clears
 * the bit and unwants it, as f_280f68 does. Switch: U3MP_MULTI_ALL=0 (eb[1] bit27, the g001 switch) leaves it out.
 * Diagnostics m01_d (EXT_BSS): [0] wants made, [1] keep bits set on an existing entry, [2] NetShutdown unwants,
 * [3] last want entry flags | level state << 8 (0xff.. = no level entry yet; state 8 = loaded). */
