/* ===== agent I i001: LIST_PLAYERS (the PARTY box) ported from PS3 1.19 f_35350c, its row click f_2844fc, row model f_334838 =====
 * PS3 1.19 map (TOC r30 of f_35350c = 0x114735c):
 *  - datasource 1.19 enum 0xb2 = f_35350c (PS4 enum 0xad, a RET stub at 0x76c4c0; the helper retags it to 0x4c414ead).
 *  - row model: f_334838 (op 9) = f_380fc8(party session 0x124b8f0 = PS4 0x17dc298, table 0x1243a34, 1), then one row
 *    {member index, guest 0} per member and a second {index, 1} when its member data byte +0x19 (the splitscreen guest
 *    NpId) is set: rows 0x1243aac (8 bytes each), count 0x1243aa8, selected row 0x1243b2c (op 5 / op 10).
 *  - f_380fc8(S, list, 1): the valid members (+0x670 + i*0x180, active +0xe0 = PS4 +0x680 + i*0x120, active +0x25), each keyed
 *    by its team (member data +9 from f_380eb0 = PS4 0x7a3400, or the net player's colour slot +0x124 = PS4 +0x21c from
 *    f_304160 = ec_find_np), then sorted by f_37f338: the host (S+0x16f8 = PS4 +0x12e8) first, then the host's team, then the
 *    rest in member order.
 *  - op 21 (focusable) and op 8 answer 1. op 11 query 0 answers 1, query 1 the connection state f_39f0c4(member +0xf0 = PS4
 *    +0x34) (PS3 ev[0xf] / ev[0xb] = PS4 ev[0x13] / ev[0xe]).
 *  - op 20 (0x353c28) row colour, selector ev+72 (PS4 ev[0x16]) == 2, colour ev+48 (PS4 ev[0xf]):
 *      net +980 (PS4 0x17d603c) != 2 -> text "" and value 0;
 *      co-op type (f_310c68) with fewer than 2 party members (f_3806c8 = PS4 0x7a2b10) -> no answer;
 *      md = f_380eb0(S, member); team = md[9]; colour = team ? (f_3133e0(team-1) & 0xffffff) | 0x80000000 : 0x80000000
 *        (f_3133e0 = PS4 0x7418e0(out, NGM, index, 0), colour at out+0xc; colour-blind aware through 0x17b6368+0x5244);
 *      guest rows of 2-member parties in 2-team games swap the index (team-1 == 0 ? 1 : 0) when f_31089c or the type is
 *        18 / 10 (dead on PS4: no second local user, so no guest rows);
 *      then the match member with the same name (f_37fb00 on g_matchSession 0x12405f8 = PS4 0x17d6420) -> its net player
 *        f_3097d0(NGM, id +0xe8 = PS4 +0x2c) (guest: f_30a148) -> colour slot +0x124 (PS4 +0x21c) >= 0 overrides the colour.
 *    PS4 reads the net game index NGM+0x661c in 0x7418e0 / 0x7210a0, unset in the LAN lobby (v5.43): it is substituted with
 *    the custom game's selection 0x17d167c for the call, as r2_team_source does.
 *  - row click 0x3406420c (PS3 registration 0x282120 -> f_2844fc; PS4 0x674120 -> 0x671d00). PS4's 0x671d00 reads the member
 *    table at 0x13a60e0, which no PS4 code writes (the filler went with the RET stub) and which the linker put in the read-only
 *    text segment, so a member row would read a null member. Replaced by i01_click (x-stub 0x16980, kind 221), the LAN branch of
 *    f_2844fc: the online branch (net +0x3c = PS4 +0x40) stays PS4's own 0x671b40 as in 0x671d00.
 * Team source: R2 Change Team (PS4 native 0x754d30 op 13) writes profile +0x77c and calls 0x74c980, which rebuilds the member
 * data (+9 = team) and stores it with 0x7a32d0 (session +0x12f0 / +0x12f4 for this PC): the next frame's op 20 reads it.
 * Focus (i01_focus, from op 6 every frame on the page that shows the box): PS4 pages activate (0x623520) before their own
 * list reports rows, so focus falls through to the box (the reason it was kept unfocusable since v4.48). For 120 frames after
 * a page activation or a popup closing (unless the box had focus before the popup), a focus that lands on the box moves to the
 * first focusable control before it in page order (PS3: the page's first control). The profile box (0x649e809a, focusable on
 * PS4 whenever it has a title) hands its focus on the same way (Left from the box), else to the box.
 * Switches: U3MP_PARTY119=0 (eb[1] bit16, and the builder leaves 0x671d00 alone): the old interim source and click;
 *           U3MP_PARTY_FOCUS=0 (eb[1] bit17): the box stays unfocusable (op 21 = 0, no focus guard);
 * Diagnostics i01_d (EXT_BSS): [0] row refreshes, [1] rows, [2] op 20 colour answers, [3] last {team | index << 8 | np slot << 16
 * (0xff none) | row << 24}, [4] clicks, [5] last click {row | items << 8 | self << 16 | lan << 24}, [6] focus moves off the box,
 * [7] profile-box hand-offs, [8] member data missing for a row, [9] last colour value. */
