/* ===== agent J j001: Statistics card (PAGE 0x83f24f04) as PS3 1.19 f_20e450 draws it =====
 * Four causes; three are builder patches (see build_u3_profile_probe.py, agent J stubs), one is here.
 *  1. Name "garbage glyphs": PS3 f_20e450 fills its name buffer with f_364678(profile, buf) (0x20e578): the viewed NpId at
 *     profile +0x7940 (PS4 +0x7ac0), or the local user's NpId when that is empty. PS4's build 0x61cc40 lost that call: its
 *     name buffer [rbp-0x88] is never written (only strlen 0x61d4c0 and the copy 0x61da19 read it), so the card shows stack
 *     bytes. Builder: x-stub 0x16a80 at 0x61d4c0 copies the 0x24-byte NpId from +0x7ac0 (own name 0x17d6010 when empty).
 *     Switch U3MP_STATS_NAME=0.
 *  2. Values "missing": they are drawn, but off the panel. Every row is a horizontal layout node {label, value 100x30 aligned
 *     right}. In the layout engine's second pass (PS4 0x65c5f0 = PS3 f_270f20) PS3 lays each flexible child out with the
 *     share (W - fixed widths) / n, PS4 with child width + share, so a row is label-width too wide and the value lands at
 *     label end + W - 100 (the staggered "0"s right of the panel in g5i 031). The measure (0x61f7a0, width 700) grows the
 *     same way, which made the card wider than PS3's. Builder: PS3's rule at 0x65cb05 / 0x65cc5d (flexible -> share; fixed
 *     -> share, 0 when its width is 0) and 0x65ce3d / 0x65cf05 (no flexible child -> share). Switch U3MP_LAYOUT119=0.
 *  3. Rows: PS3 1.19 table 0xdb57b0 has 7 competitive rows (Objective Points 0xf84a8361 / stat 0x194 last) and 0xdb5780 5 co-op
 *     rows; PS4's 0x13a5e60 / 0x13a5e90 have 6 + 6 (Objective Points moved to the co-op list). Builder: PS3's 12 pairs
 *     written over PS4's 12, co-op base 0x13a5e98, loop limits 14 / 10. Switch U3MP_STATS_ROWS119=0.
 *  4. The rank badge (item 0x29) is drawn only while the load state is 3 (0x61d0b1, PS3 0x20e630). In g5i it was missing, so
 *     the state i05_stats set was gone by the time the card was drawn (a later activation 0x61ca20 resets it to 0, or the
 *     inline getter's offline reset sets 2). j01_tick (per frame, kind 16) puts the record back and the state to 3 while the
 *     card is up with i05_vp. Switch U3MP_STATS_KEEP=0 (eb[1] bit20).
 * Diagnostics j01_d: [0] state re-asserts, [1] last state seen before a re-assert (0 = re-activated, 2 = getter reset),
 * [2] frames the card was seen with state 3, [3] what the card holds (1 own record, 2 defaults), [4] last page seen while armed. */
