/* ===== agent J j010: in-match HUD too bright vs Uncharted 3 (user, v6.18): the PS4 UI has two passes with different gamma =====
 * Measured (user's Fort HUD vs PS3 ps3vid2 f085, whose levels match the direct PS3 captures: panel 44,18,1 vs 45,20,0):
 * every queued-UI element comes out as the sRGB encode of PS3's value: score plates PS3 59,84,26 / 109,33,37 -> encode
 * 131,154,90 / 173,100,106, ours 128,147,84 / 179,111,102; HUD text PS3 200 / 217 -> encode 228 / 237, ours 229 / 241. The
 * menu (immediate) pass has no encode: batch86 measured texels sRGB-decoded with no re-encode and constant colours unchanged
 * (panel 35,16,0 / ours 47,21,0 vs PS3 45,20,0). So:
 *  - queued UI pass (the null-context path 0xe42310 -> queue 0x18c8700; HUD sprites 0x11b8dd0 / hud-settings elements
 *    0x11b8af0, PS3 f_9936e0 / f_994a98): output is sRGB-encoded. PS3-correct inputs there are sRGB-flagged textures (decode
 *    then encode = PS3's raw texel) and sRGB-decoded constant colours.
 *  - immediate UI pass (menus, the UI quad 0x63dc40): no encode. PS3-correct inputs are raw (UNORM) textures and raw colours.
 * batch86 made the shared colour maps UNORM (hud.pak general/hud/guns/*, all of net.pak), right for menus, wrong for the HUD.
 * Fix (two parts, each switchable; meant to go with batch86 removed, i.e. the sRGB flags back in the paks):
 *  (1) HUD colours: value stub kind 229 at 0x11b8dd0 (sprite draw): with a null context (queued pass) and MP active, the
 *      colour argument (rcx -> float4) is replaced by a decoded copy (exact sRGB curve, 257-entry table, alpha unchanged).
 *      Switch U3MP_HUD_GAMMA=0 (eb[2] bit0).
 *  (2) Menu textures: in the UI quad's batch hook (kind 165, 0x63dcbb, before j004), with MP active and a draw context (rsi;
 *      0x63dcc3 sends context-less quads to the queued pass, left alone), an image handle whose
 *      texture object is type 3 (T# at [obj+8], copied by the resource writer 0xe66aa8 without the executor's type-2 mask)
 *      with num_format sRGB (T# word 1 bits 26..29 = 9) is replaced by a helper handle -> type-3 object -> a copy of that T#
 *      with num_format 0 (UNORM): menus sample raw texels as with batch86, the pak keeps sRGB for the HUD. 48 cached copies,
 *      refreshed every draw. Switch U3MP_MENU_UNORM=0 (eb[2] bit1).
 * Not covered: HUD text (font path 0xf1d9f0 with its own colour block) and HUD quads that push the queue inline (HUD code
 * 0xc3fb9d..0xc4838f); j10_d tells whether they matter.
 * j10_d: [0] sprite calls, [1] colours decoded, [2] sprite calls with a context (left), [3] UI-quad calls, [4] handles
 * replaced, [5] handles not sRGB (left), [6] handles not type 3 (left), [7] cache entries, [8] last replaced T# word 1,
 * [9] last left T# word 1, [10] cache evictions, [11] context-less UI quads (queued pass, left). */
