/* ===== agent M m003 (3): Find Game, spoofed matchmaking for testing (user request; U3MP_MM_SPOOF, default on) =====
 * With no community server (offline mode, b044) Find Game showed PS3's network-failure dialog. With U3MP_MM_SPOOF it runs PS3
 * 1.19's real flow and its real UI, and only the matchmaking data is faked. All of the fake part is in this block.
 *  1. Find Game: the b016 online branch (PS3 1.19 0x290a1c): net mode 1 (0x17d603c), menu user 0, PAGE_PLAYLISTS 0x0b7714b5.
 *     The playlist list is PS4's native enum 0x24 (0x752630 = 1.19 f_341570): DC 0xc1b0be0d, filtered as on PS3 (content
 *     flag; with the LAN flag set, the co-op byte must match, so competitive lists competitive playlists).
 *  2. BUTTON_MULTIPLAYER_STARTMATCH (kind 9 -> start_game) in net mode 1 = PS3 1.19 f_2986c0 0x29871c..0x2989bc: clear V[0..1]
 *     (0x1241d48 = PS4 0x17d7760), party unlock when leader (f_37f3a8(s,0)), party message 0x114 (backend; nothing offline), popup
 *     "Starting in [A]..." 0x73a73dd8 for 2 s with ok 0x4055f45f (PS4 named callback 0x66ed20: back history, net state 20,
 *     PAGE_MULTIPLAYER_MATCHMAKING 0xe35f0f1a, 0x751aa0(0xe35f0f1a, 0xea2119f2), 0x16e7171 = 0x101) and cancel 0xbbb649ef (0x66ed90).
 *     Not ported: the party-size / DLC dialogs (one player, every DLC owned) and f_37efec(match, playlist) - the real
 *     matchmaking request, which the spoof replaces.
 *  3. The spoof (m03_tick, per frame, from the popup's ok until the match starts or the player backs out) drives the variables
 *     PS4's own matchmaking UI reads, in PS3's order:
 *     - net +0x40 (0x17d5c98; PS3 net +0x3c, f_325584 = "matchmaking active") = status: 1 searching, 2 "Voting starts in [A]...",
 *       6 "GAME STARTING IN [A]...", deadline net +0x2c (0x17d5c84) on the net clock *(0x17c3580)+0xc, 300/s;
 *     - search phase index 0x17d79e8 into DC 0xb25ab071 ("Searching for Optimal Game" / "Close Game" / "Any Game") while net +0x18
 *       (0x17d5c70) is 0, then net +0x18 = 1: "Searching for players...". The texts come from PS4's status source 0x75c190
 *       (enum 0x4f = 1.19 f_352a94), which PS3 shows as the title of LIST_PLAYERS while matchmaking.
 *     - LIST_PLAYERS: PS3 1.19 f_35350c hands every op to f_352e58 while f_325584(net); f_352e58 lists the matchmaking slots
 *       (0x1241d88, 0x20 bytes each, count +0x140): kind 2 = a member (name, rank badge 0xf5a294f3 type 0x29, team colour),
 *       kind 1 = "Found Player" 0xa91680a8, kind 0 = "Finding Player..." 0xc0759450 with icon type 16. Ported as m03_players with
 *       the fake slots: row 0 = this profile, then "Player 2".. as they are "found" (one every 1.2 s, each shown 0.6 s as Found
 *       Player), up to the playlist's maximum (entry +0x1c, at most 10).
 *  4. When the countdown ends (U3MP_MM_SPOOF_START, default on) a local match starts like Custom Game: a net game of the playlist
 *     picked by its weights (entry +0x30: {n, ptr} of {net game id, weight}; record = DC 0x3b9a067d entry with that id at +0),
 *     SelectNetGame(mgr, idx, 0, 0xc), net mode 2, status 0, then start_game_now (session reset + countdown done 0x66e9b0) on the
 *     LAN backend that offline mode runs. With U3MP_MM_SPOOF_START=0 the page stays at "Waiting for players..." (status 5).
 *  Cancel: backing out (Circle) to PAGE_PLAYLISTS / PAGE_MULTIPLAYER stops the spoof: status 0, net +0x18 = 0, net state 3.
 *  Scope: offline mode only (onb_mode 2); a configured community server keeps the real path. On the PC (LAN flag set) PS4's
 *  tab bar / LIST_MATCHMAKING / tips sources find no tab config (DC 0xf1514340 has the matchmaking page only for LAN 0), so
 *  they stay empty; the title (playlist name), the status and the players list are shown.
 * Switches: U3MP_MM_SPOOF=0 (bit5): the failure dialog again; U3MP_MM_SPOOF_START=0 (bit6): no match at the end.
 * Diagnostics m03_d: [0] STARTMATCH presses, [1] spoof runs, [2] phase, [3] players found, [4] cancels, [5] matches started,
 * [6] picked net game index, [7] list asks. */
