/* ===== agent L l001: everything unlocked from rank 1; LAN profiles at max prestige / level with the co-op star and the ND paw =====
 * Switch byte rw2+0x405a (= ExtState eb[2] bits 16..23, agent L). All parts default ON; a set bit turns that part off.
 *  bit16 U3MP_UNLOCK_ALL=0   unlock manager (PS3 1.19 f_39b238 = PS4 0x7bb5b0): every unlock condition passes, and the items are
 *                            owned (free). The builder's x-stub at the evaluator entry (slot 0x17280+0) answers 1 for every cond
 *                            type 1..7 and >= 8 (rank, rank<, trophy, treasure set, item, DLC pack incl. c012's 0x100..0x3ff, legacy)
 *                            while the bit is clear; with the bit set (or U3MP_UNLOCK_ALL=0 at build time) the native body runs,
 *                            c012's cond-6 stub included. The new-item marker callers (return address in 0x7bd0b0..0x7bde8f:
 *                            notify, is-new 0x7bd6f0, mark-seen 0x7bda50, has-new 0x7bdc70) get 0 instead, so the unlocked items
 *                            carry no "!" and no seen bit is written (bit21 U3MP_UNLOCK_NEW=1: they get 1 too). Ownership/price: l01_tick raises the game's own "Give all Store Items"
 *                            bool 0x17b2a94 (PS3 0x11ce9e4) every frame, the switch the unlock manager tests first: 0x7bba70
 *                            answers owned, so the item status 0x7bca00 is 0 (owned: no price, no "can't afford", nothing bought,
 *                            cash untouched, no owned bit written to the profile), the row filter 0x7be0b0 hides nothing (type-6
 *                            DLC rows included), booster tiers (0x6882b0/0x689088) and kickback levels (0x74eba0) are the maximum.
 *                            U3MP_UNLOCK_STORE (s010) raises the same bool; both must be 0 for PS3's rank/price progression.
 *  bit17 U3MP_MAX_RANK=0     on every LAN profile load (mp_profile_start, competitive and co-op files): legacy (record +0x1618) =
 *                            5 (1.19 cap, f_365674 / f_366b60; 3 when U3MP_LEGACY119=0) and XP (+0x4fc, +0x500) = the level-75
 *                            threshold of DC 0xc85e199d at that legacy (f_5c11c: x5.0 at legacy 5), so f_5c210 gives level index
 *                            74 = rank 75 everywhere the game computes the rank (profile box, party row, Statistics card, lobby,
 *                            HUD/scoreboard art ranks/prestige-75, records page prestige-back-5).
 *  bit18 U3MP_COOP_STAR=0    co-op adventure word +0x1624 |= 0x1f (all five adventures; PS3 f_320dxx sets 1 << map, star when
 *                            (w & 0x1f) == 0x1f: f_365500 0x3655e0, PS4 0x782091 / 0x6b8022 / 0x74cc5b). Also fixes a009's kind 64,
 *                            which read the big-endian byte +0x1627 (on PS4 the word is little-endian: the bits are at +0x1624).
 *  bit19 U3MP_ND_PAW=0       record +0x1f1c = 1 (1.19 f_365500: paw = +0x1f1c != 0 -> rank value bit 30, f_2590d4). PS4 never reads
 *                            or writes +0x1f1c (no disp 0x1f1c/0x2164 in the image), so the field is free.
 *  bit22 U3MP_MAX_RANK_ONLINE=1  bits 17..19 also for the profile Play Online loads (default: LAN Party only, 0x17d5c60 != 0 at
 *                            mp_profile_start, so the community server / leaderboards keep the real rank).
 *  bit20 U3MP_BADGE_LAYERS=0 menu rank badge drawn in PS3 1.19's layers (type-0x29 drawer around 0x263510..0x263890): prestige-back-
 *                            <legacy> behind the art (legacy 1..5), the art, the co-op star general/net/rank-badges/coop-star (sid
 *                            0x0242a063, UI texture table) in the bottom-right quarter, ranks/ndpaw-icon in the bottom-left quarter
 *                            (PS3 rects: k = -0.5 at r30-32684: star (x+w/2, y+h/2)-(x+w, y+h), paw (x, y+h/2)-(x+w/2, y+h)).
 *                            rank_icon_as_texture tags its type-2 answer (item +0x10 = 'B10L', +0x14 = rank value; type 2 never
 *                            reads them); the builder hooks the type-2 quad call 0x64228e (call 0x63dc40, only caller) -> slot 0x17280+0x40 -> kind 230.
 * Saved files: the record format is unchanged. mp_publish writes the profile's own values of the five fields (XP = own XP + XP earned
 * since the load), so switching l001 off brings the real rank back. Diagnostics l01_d (see NOTES-l001.md for the peek address). */
