/* ===== fixer H h004: MP particle modules part-multiplayer + part-obj-shade-char (kickback activation glow, PS3 1.19 NetInit) =====
 * PS3 1.19 kickback activation f_36ae1c (PS4 0x791380.., ported 1:1 by Bluepoint): kickback entry (net.bin 0xd9f6ada2, +0x10
 * type) -> colour: weapon 0xd862a057 = (0.04, 1, 0.07) green (RPG!!!), standard 0x13a1c349 = (1, 0.65, 0.1) gold, grenade
 * 0x31f143bf = (1, 0.07, 0.04) red (Quick Boom, Mega Bomb, ...); type 0 = no glow; booster 0xa3ac029b forces gold. Then a
 * particle process "medal-streak-active-tier3" on joint spinec (0x119b250 with info {0x68a84033, 0x08556eeb, ... 0xabe8fb6b})
 * and the colour into its +0x50 (PS3 f_979334). Code and colours are identical on PS4 (0x1402810/20/30 = PS3 TOC consts).
 * The effect lives in the part module part-multiplayer (sid 0x666e04e1; PS4 dc2/part-module/part-multiplayer.bin has 173 of
 * PS3's 178 symbols, all but skelzor-eyes). PS3 only loads it from the net code: f_28f7.. (0x28fae0..0x28fb48) every update
 * "if (!requested) RequestModule" for part-multiplayer and part-obj-shade-char (0x4be4375d), and NetShutdown f_280f68
 * (0x28122c..0x281254) releases both. PS4 has no reference to either sid (no level, pak or DC module list names them), so
 * every part-multiplayer effect fails to spawn in MP: the kickback glow, grenade-quick-boom-indicator, marked-man-active,
 * mega-bomb / super-grenade indicators, kickback-healing / speedy / distruption / smoke-bomb / crawlies / skeleton-transition,
 * the nav-waypoint rings and pillars, treasure-capture bursts, kickback-chest-open, mod-laser, idol-curse ...
 * PS4 moved part modules out of the ScriptManager into the particle manager 0x1a4d910: its want map (+0x50, refcounted,
 * FNV-1a(sid) % [+0x4c] buckets at [+0x10], node {next, .., +0x10 sid, +0x18 refs}) is fed by the level loader (0x10f4322,
 * level info +0xc8 list) and fma-request-part-module (0xc6b2f7); 0xeb4110 = want (refs+1), 0xeb41e0 = unwant; the loaded
 * table is +0x298 (stride 0x30, count +0x8c8), read by part-module-loaded? (0xc6ae50).
 * h04_tick (per-frame tick, kind 16) = PS3's polls: while MP is active (0x17d5c61) each module not in the want map is wanted;
 * when MP ends (NetShutdown point clears 0x17d5c61) the modules the helper wanted are unwanted again.
 * Switch U3MP_PARTMP119=0 -> ExtState.ec[1] bit3. Diagnostics ec[204..209] (see NOTES-h004). */
