/* ===== fixer L n032: Profile > Records rows and the player card's Competitive / Co-op tabs while the LAN byte is set =====
 * (1) Records. PS3 1.19 LIST_RECORDS f_34f074 (enum 0xcc) picks its rows by the LAN byte (1.19 [0x123ef88]+4 = PS4 0x17d5c60):
 *     set -> table 0xdb9bc4, 3 rows (Medals 0x44834c35, Tips 0x675b2d54, Legacy 0x2b9634d5); clear (online) -> table 0xdb9bf4,
 *     8 rows: Missions 0xcb925f92 (button 0xe4794ab9 -> PAGE_MISSIONS 0xdfdb36fa), Treasures 0x87007e8a (0xe9bce205 ->
 *     PAGE_NET_TREASURE_SETS), Medals, Trophies 0xf1b9728c (0x7a95893b), Tips (page 0x7fe5986f), Message of the Day 0xa6694384
 *     (page 0x2f2041a5), Tournament 0xc3d9ca3f (page 0xe34c6094), Legacy (0xa0bacf62). The user's PS3 shot is the online list.
 *     PS4 0x76e460 keeps the same choice (0x76e50f: LAN -> 0x13a65f0, 3 rows; else 0x13a6620, 5 rows = PS3's online table
 *     without Trophies / Message of the Day / Tournament: PS4 has no handler or page for them (no 0x7a95893b anywhere, pages
 *     0x2f2041a5 / 0xe34c6094 are in neither the retail nor the installed menu.bin; Tournament is also a user "no").
 *     LAN Party and offline mode run with the LAN byte set, so the list had only Medals / Tips / Legacy. While n32_records
 *     holds, records_source answers the online 5 rows: Missions, Treasures, Medals, Tips, Legacy. Rows 2..4 are the LAN
 *     table's rows 0..2 (same entries), so the native answers them with the index moved by 2; rows 0 / 1 are answered here as
 *     the native answers its online rows (op 2 text, no op 4 icon: mask 0, op 21 text id, op 22 button 0x64ce90(menu, +8, 0)).
 *     op 6 = native + 2 (it already drops Legacy when the profile cannot legacy). The native's page/tab check
 *     (DC 0xf1514340, Records tab 0x5ed0426e) keeps reading the real LAN byte, so the tab state is untouched.
 *     The click targets are already ported: catch_all 0xe4794ab9 -> PAGE_MISSIONS (LIST_MISSIONS = missions_source),
 *     0xe9bce205 -> PAGE_NET_TREASURE_SETS (menu.bin button / catch_all); both pages have their LAN tab rows in the DC.
 * (2) Player card PAGE_PLAYER_PROFILE 0x83f24f04 (party row > Statistics; card build 0x61cc40 = PS3 1.19 f_20e450). Its tab
 *     bar (0xaec943f5, enum 0xc3 = 0x76bbf0, param 0x83f24f04: Competitive 0xc5a3c7e3 / Co-op 0x5ca3366e) and the card body
 *     (0xbe8cdd10, enum 0xde = 0x76fa00: page count = tab rows, op 5 = the selected tab) find their row in DC 0xf1514340 by
 *     {page, LAN byte}; net.bin has only the LAN-byte-0 entry for 0x83f24f04 (retail PS4 and the installed e8524231 alike),
 *     so with the byte set there were no tabs and the body never switched. Both widgets are retagged (0xcf / 0x4e4e32c3,
 *     0x4e4e32de) and run their natives with the LAN byte cleared for the call (n003 / m005 pattern). Both use the same
 *     DC entry, so the selected tab (entry +0x18) is shared as on PS3 online. 0x61cc40 reads the tab from the body control
 *     (vcalls 0 / 0x38 / 0x40): 0 = Competitive (Time Played rec+0x5b8 + 7 rows), 1 = Co-op (rec+0x5c0 + 5 rows) = f_20e450.
 * Switch word ExtState ea[122] (builder): bit0 U3MP_RECORDS119=0 (3 LAN rows), bit1 U3MP_CARD_TABS=0 (no retag, native),
 * bit2 U3MP_N032_OFFLINE_ONLY=1 (both parts only in offline mode; LAN Party then as PS3 1.19 LAN).
 * Diagnostics: ea[125] Records count answers (low 16) | rows 0/1 clicks << 16; ea[127] card tab / body calls run as online
 * (low 24) | retags << 24. Peek n32=20ebe38:0x18 (ea[122..127]; ea[123] / ea[124] are n024's). */
