/* ===== coop-visual-v7106 grab g006: grabbed player, fist icon and blue HUD name, boot.log lines =====
 * Script (PS3 1.19 DC = recipe overlay-r3 dc1/ps4/ss-multiplayer/ss-npc-grapple.bin, same on both): state "grappling",
 * entry track 3: animate(player, 0xa5a9314a, ap-ref), wait-animate(self = the grabber, 0xbcf6378a, get-grapple-ap-ref),
 * THEN set-focusable-grappled(player, #t) (the only writer of player +0x39c bit 2 = PS3 +664 bit 5, PS4 0xc71702, PS3
 * 0x812c0; not carried by the net player update on either: PS3 0x2d5d68 / PS4 0x718953 copy bits 0, 1, 3 only) and
 * set-boolean 0xff6b803a; the update track calls net-hud-set-grapple-indicator(net-id, t) every frame (-> HUD element
 * mode 2, blue ring + PS3's fist, PS4 0xc2c6ad / 0xc2d11f) independently of that wait. The TEAM LIVES name turns blue
 * (0xff0000f0, grapple icon) only from bit 2 (PS4 0xc3488f, PS3 f_665adc): so the ring can be up while the name stays
 * green when the script never gets past the wait-animate on that machine, or sets the bit on another object.
 * Lines (all "U3MP grab:", at most 80 in all, frame = 0x17b4a90+0x214):
 *   wrappers N/4               natives_link re-pointed N of the 4 records (4 = all logging in place)
 *   indicator net-id I trk T   net-hud-set-grapple-indicator ran (start of a grab on this machine), T = tracker or -1
 *   ap-ref ret R trk T         get-grapple-ap-ref(grabber, player) answered R (0 = no ap: the anims have no anchor)
 *   wait-animate ret R         the grabber's wait-animate 0xbcf6378a was called (again = still waiting, if it polls)
 *   set-focusable-grappled .. the native ran: obj, value (1 on / 0 off), tracker of that obj (-1 = not a HUD tracker
 *                              player: the name cannot turn blue), the player's +0x39c byte after it (bit 0x04 = blue)
 *   ring up: slot sid S idx I  first mode-2 icon call of a grab: S should be 0x76d3d726 (coop-icons/grapple); I = -1
 *                              means the init cached no index (the v7.101 refusal case, now looked up by sid)
 *   material M                 0 = the grapple texture is not in the class-1 dictionary (net.pak not loaded / missing)
 *   icon drawn h H a A         first fist drawn in that grab, half size and alpha as float bits (a 0 = invisible)
 *   tracker T flags F          a tracker player's +0x39c byte changed while a mode-2 ring is up (0x04 set = blue name)
 *   ring gone after N calls, D drawn   printed at the next grab's start for the previous one */
